From b9fa8893102dc3bbcec92762230e7f1678644a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Penny <Pennyroyal@agentmail.to>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:32:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] perf(moe): fold the fused-finalize output zeroing into
 the activation kernel

Direct port of the published donor patch, kept at the text level: every
added and removed line of the two csrc files is line-for-line the donor's,

  aiueo52/flash-next-rtxpro6000 @ e0fa9fa9fc3ccd710a8fb3d2639b85ce62188c23
  patches/flashinfer/03-g2-1-fold-finalize-memset.patch

(wheel-side flashinfer/data/csrc/... paths map 1:1 to this repo's
csrc/... paths).  doActivationKernel now takes [fused_zero_ptr,
fused_zero_ptr + 16 * fused_zero_vec16) and zeroes it with uint4 stores in
a grid-stride loop *before* cudaGridDependencySynchronize(), and gemm2
skips cudaMemsetAsync(final_output, 0x0, ...) when it handed the activation
kernel that buffer, removing one launch from the serial
GEMM1 -> activation -> GEMM2 chain.  Donor algorithm, synchronisation,
guards, alignment checks and fallback are as supplied:
FLASHINFER_MOE_FOLD_MEMSET=0 restores the standalone memset, the fold
still requires the fused-finalize GEMM2 tactic, a TMA-warp-specialized
GEMM1 config, a gated activation, no LoRA, no W4AFP8 and no fp8
block-scale runner, and it stands down unless the finalize region is a
multiple of 16 B and final_output is 16B-aligned.  Rejected A3 stride
fusion is absent (no FLASHINFER_MOE_FUSED_STRIDES anywhere in the tree) and
this commit stands on the accepted A0 base alone.

Mechanical 0.7 adaptations, the donor preimage being an older wheel-side
copy; the ladder of changes is signature-shape only:

* The 0.7 doActivationKernel/doActivation parameter lists carry
  permuted_token_selected_experts, fp8_token_dequant_scale and
  fp8_expert_residual_scale, so five touched lines are the base line plus
  the donor's addition rather than the donor's text.  Two of them
  re-wrapped under the repo .clang-format (ColumnLimit 100).
* The base's lora bias epilogue call passes the extra activation arguments
  as the donor's did not, so its explicit "no fold" arguments are
  `..., enable_pdl, stream, nullptr, 0`.
* The run() insertion point is the same: after the fc1-side
  applyPrequantScale(smoothed_act_, permuted_data_, ..., hidden_size,
  use_awq, ...) and its sync_check_cuda_error, before Self::gemm1.
* gemm1/gemm2 keep their new arguments defaulted in the header
  declaration, so the min-latency call sites and the GEMM profiler path
  (which must keep its own memset while timing tactics) are unchanged.

Applicability on the intended SM120 profile, checked in the base sources:
the profile reaches the CUTLASS runner through isNvfp4Quant() as
CutlassMoeFCRunner<Fp4Type, Fp4Type>, where use_fp4 holds and
use_w4afp8 / use_wfp4a16 / blockscale_gemm_runner do not, so every donor
gate is openable; GEMM2 finalize-fusion tactics are enumerated
(getTactics(GEMM_2) -> getTmaWarpSpecializedConfigs(..., FINALIZE
duplicates)) because mayHaveFinalizeFused() holds for that instantiation
on SM120.  Two base gates are worth naming for review: (1) a bf16-
activation W4A16 runner (WeightType Fp4Type with T bf16) sets
use_sm90_mixed_input_gemm, which mayHaveFinalizeFused() rejects, so there
is no fused finalize and nothing to fold on that instantiation at all;
(2) the untuned default GEMM2 tactic is mAllProfiles[gemm1_tactic_count],
the first candidate, which is a *non*-finalize config, so the memset --
and therefore this optimization -- is only in play when a finalize-fusion
tactic is chosen (autotune or explicit profile_ids).  The new test runs the
autotuner for that reason.  One behaviour change to note: the zeroing used
to be a stream-ordered memset, which cannot start until everything earlier
in the stream has finished; the folded version runs before
cudaGridDependencySynchronize(), so under PDL it is separated from the
previous call's GEMM2 only by the launch chain.  The repeated-call arm of
the test is the check for that, and the kill switch is the escape hatch.

New GPU regression tests/moe/test_cutlass_fused_moe_g21_fold_memset.py
reuses the accepted A0 NVFP4 harness (same 512-expert / top-10 route
shapes, same helpers, subprocess arms per kill-switch value) and makes
three observations per case instead of trusting the flag: launched device
ops must contain doActivationKernel (the fold's host kernel) and must not
contain finalizeMoeRouting*Kernel (the fused epilogue was chosen, so an
output zeroing exists), and the folded arm must show exactly one fewer
device memset than FLASHINFER_MOE_FOLD_MEMSET=0 -- an unpatched build or a
shape that fails the gate shows equal counts and fails rather than passing
vacuously.  Both arms are called twice into one reused output buffer and
compared with the same torch NVFP4 reference, so output that is not
re-zeroed (the second call accumulating onto the first) is detectable; a
use_fused_finalize=False case pins memset counts and results as identical
across the two arms, which is the fallback-preservation check.

Not run here: room101 has no GPU, no CUDA toolkit, no pytest and no
tvm_ffi.  Checked on room101: python -m py_compile of the new test, a
symbol cross-check of every imported helper (A0 module and
test_trtllm_cutlass_fused_moe), a line-by-line diff of this commit against
the donor patch (only the five documented 0.7 signature lines differ), and
greps proving no A3 or other donor patch leaked in.  Compilation and the
SM120 pytest arms are for the thegrid run.
---
 .../cutlass_fused_moe_kernels.cuh             | 74 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../cutlass_kernels/include/moe_kernels.h     |  9 ++-
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/csrc/fused_moe/cutlass_backend/cutlass_fused_moe_kernels.cuh b/csrc/fused_moe/cutlass_backend/cutlass_fused_moe_kernels.cuh
index 60ed9b8..b43cf5a 100644
--- a/csrc/fused_moe/cutlass_backend/cutlass_fused_moe_kernels.cuh
+++ b/csrc/fused_moe/cutlass_backend/cutlass_fused_moe_kernels.cuh
@@ -2408,6 +2408,16 @@ void doGatedActivation(ActivationOutputType* output, GemmOutputType const* gemm_
 
 // ============================== Activation =================================
 
+// G2-1: FLASHINFER_MOE_FOLD_MEMSET=0 keeps the fused-finalize output zeroing as its own
+// cudaMemsetAsync launch instead of folding it into doActivationKernel's grid.
+inline bool foldMemsetEnabled() {
+  static bool const enabled = [] {
+    char const* v = std::getenv("FLASHINFER_MOE_FOLD_MEMSET");
+    return !(v && v[0] == '0' && v[1] == '\0');
+  }();
+  return enabled;
+}
+
 template <class T, class GemmOutputType, class ScaleBiasType, class ActFn,
           TmaWarpSpecializedGroupedGemmInput::FpXBlockScalingType BlockScalingType,
           bool DISABLE_FP4_QUANT_FAST_MATH = false, typename NVFP4_4OVER6_CONFIG = std::false_type>
@@ -2417,7 +2427,8 @@ __global__ __launch_bounds__(MAX_ACTIVATION_THREADS_PER_BLOCK) void doActivation
     int const* permuted_token_selected_experts, int num_experts_per_node, int64_t inter_size,
     float const* fc2_act_global_scale, bool use_per_expert_act_scale,
     TmaWarpSpecializedGroupedGemmInput::ElementSF* fc2_act_sf_flat, float* fp8_token_dequant_scale,
-    float const* fp8_expert_residual_scale, ActivationParams activation_params) {
+    float const* fp8_expert_residual_scale, ActivationParams activation_params,
+    void* fused_zero_ptr, int64_t fused_zero_vec16) {
 #ifdef ENABLE_FP4
   constexpr bool IsNVFP4 =
       std::is_same_v<T, Fp4Type> &&
@@ -2455,6 +2466,20 @@ __global__ __launch_bounds__(MAX_ACTIVATION_THREADS_PER_BLOCK) void doActivation
 
   int64_t const num_valid_tokens = expert_first_token_offset[num_experts_per_node];
 
+  // G2-1: fold the fused-finalize output zeroing (a 1.0 us memset32 launch in the serial MoE
+  // chain) into this kernel.  It is placed *before* cudaGridDependencySynchronize() because the
+  // zeroing depends on nothing GEMM1 produces; the stores are ordered ahead of GEMM2 by this
+  // kernel's cudaTriggerProgrammaticLaunchCompletion() below, exactly as the memset was.
+  if (fused_zero_ptr != nullptr) {
+    uint4* zero_out = reinterpret_cast<uint4*>(fused_zero_ptr);
+    uint4 const zero_val = make_uint4(0u, 0u, 0u, 0u);
+    int64_t const zero_tid = int64_t(blockIdx.x) * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;
+    int64_t const zero_stride = int64_t(gridDim.x) * blockDim.x;
+    for (int64_t i = zero_tid; i < fused_zero_vec16; i += zero_stride) {
+      zero_out[i] = zero_val;
+    }
+  }
+
 #if (defined(__CUDA_ARCH__) && (__CUDA_ARCH__ >= 900))
   cudaGridDependencySynchronize();
 #endif
@@ -2636,7 +2661,8 @@ void doActivation(T* output, GemmOutputType const* gemm_result, float const* fp8
                   QuantParams const& quant_params, bool use_per_expert_act_scale,
                   TmaWarpSpecializedGroupedGemmInput::ElementSF* fc2_act_sf_flat,
                   float* fp8_token_dequant_scale, float const* fp8_expert_residual_scale,
-                  bool enable_pdl, cudaStream_t stream) {
+                  bool enable_pdl, cudaStream_t stream, void* fused_zero_ptr = nullptr,
+                  int64_t fused_zero_vec16 = 0) {
   TLLM_CHECK_WITH_INFO(
       (inter_size * std::min(sizeof_bits<T>::value, sizeof_bits<GemmOutputType>::value)) % 128 == 0,
       "inter_size %ld rows are not a multiple of 16B; doActivationKernel requires 16B-aligned rows",
@@ -2778,7 +2804,7 @@ void doActivation(T* output, GemmOutputType const* gemm_result, float const* fp8
                      expert_first_token_offset, permuted_token_selected_experts,
                      num_experts_per_node, inter_size, quant_params.fp4.fc2.act_global_scale,
                      use_per_expert_act_scale, fc2_act_sf_flat, fp8_token_dequant_scale,
-                     fp8_expert_residual_scale, activation_type);
+                     fp8_expert_residual_scale, activation_type, fused_zero_ptr, fused_zero_vec16);
 }
 
 // ============================== Lora Add Bias =================================
@@ -3465,7 +3491,8 @@ void CutlassMoeFCRunner<
                    ActivationParams fc1_activation_type, float const** alpha_scale_ptr_array,
                    bool bias_is_broadcast, cudaStream_t stream,
                    cutlass_extensions::CutlassGemmConfig config, bool min_latency_mode,
-                   int* num_active_experts_per, int* active_expert_global_ids, bool enable_pdl) {
+                   int* num_active_experts_per, int* active_expert_global_ids, bool enable_pdl,
+                   void* fused_zero_ptr, int64_t fused_zero_vec16) {
   if (fp8_blockscale_gemm_runner) {
     TLLM_CHECK(!min_latency_mode);
     Self::BlockScaleFC1(*fp8_blockscale_gemm_runner, input, output, intermediate_result,
@@ -3561,7 +3588,7 @@ void CutlassMoeFCRunner<
         bias_is_broadcast, expert_first_token_offset, permuted_token_selected_experts,
         num_experts_per_node, inter_size, expanded_num_rows, fc1_activation_type, quant_params,
         use_per_expert_act_scale, fc2_fp4_act_flat, fp8_token_dequant_scale,
-        fp8_expert_residual_scale, enable_pdl, stream);
+        fp8_expert_residual_scale, enable_pdl, stream, fused_zero_ptr, fused_zero_vec16);
 
     sync_check_cuda_error(stream);
   } else if (use_fp8) {
@@ -3714,7 +3741,8 @@ void CutlassMoeFCRunner<T, WeightType, OutputType, InputType, BackBoneType, IsMX
           bool use_lora, void* fc2_lora, cudaStream_t stream,
           MOEParallelismConfig parallelism_config, bool const enable_alltoall,
           cutlass_extensions::CutlassGemmConfig config, bool min_latency_mode,
-          int* num_active_experts_per, int* active_expert_global_ids, bool enable_pdl) {
+          int* num_active_experts_per, int* active_expert_global_ids, bool enable_pdl,
+          bool finalize_output_prezeroed) {
   int64_t const* total_tokens_including_expert = expert_first_token_offset + 1;
 
   bool const using_tma_ws_gemm2 = gemm_runner.isTmaWarpSpecialized(config);
@@ -3746,8 +3774,11 @@ void CutlassMoeFCRunner<T, WeightType, OutputType, InputType, BackBoneType, IsMX
       //
       // This also means it is included in the timing for the profiler, which is probably more
       // representative until we can overlap it
-      check_cuda_error(cudaMemsetAsync(
-          final_output, 0x0, sizeof(OutputType) * num_rows * unpadded_hidden_size, stream));
+      // G2-1: skipped when doActivationKernel already zeroed this buffer in its own grid.
+      if (!finalize_output_prezeroed) {
